	(footprint "MOUSEBITE_6"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "079cf6b9-9712-418a-9dcc-a609897a7cf2")
		(at 45.2 35.5)
		(descr "Six 0.6 mm NPTH perforations along the write-protect tab's break line. These were previously drawn as 0.6 mm circles on Edge.Cuts, i.e. as MILLED features - and JLCPCB's minimum internal routing feature is 1.0 mm (0.8 mm at surcharge), so a 0.6 mm milled circle is below what their router can cut. They would have drawn a DFM query, been silently omitted, or broken a bit. Omitted, the tab is a solid 7.4 mm slab of FR4 and the write-protect feature is dead on every board. As drilled holes 0.6 mm is routine. Placed at x = 45.2, y = 35.5 on the board. PITCH IS 1.05 mm, giving 0.45 mm edge-to-edge between holes: at the original 0.85 mm pitch the gap was 0.25 mm, below JLCPCB's NPTH-to-NPTH minimum. As milled Edge.Cuts circles that rule never applied; drilling them brought it into scope.")
		(tags "mousebite perforation breakaway NPTH")
		(property "Reference" "MB1"
			(at 0 -1.6 0)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
